{{Evolved Card Infobox|Cost=7|CycleCost=1|Rarity=Common|Type=Troop|Arena=Royal Arena|ReleaseDate=4 September 2023}}
{{Quote|Royal Recruits have been taking lessons from Prince. Once their shields have been broken, they will begin an epic charge!}}

The Royal Recruits' Evolution is a {{Rarity|Common}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked with 6 Evolution Shards. It spawns 6 Royal Recruits with identical stats to the originals. After their shield is destroyed, they gain the ability to charge towards their target after traveling 2 tiles, dealing 2x damage if they hit the target whilst charging. They appear as men with large, round noses, wear wooden buckets with team-colored feathers, which cover their faces, metal gloves, an armor, a chainmail, a purple shirt, cape, pants and sandals, and a team-colored band on their right arm and belt with purple linings and a [[Card Evolution]] symbol in the center, and wield spears and wooden shields. The Royal Recruits' Evolution costs 7 [[Elixir]] and requires 1 cycle to deploy.

==Strategy==
*The Evolved Royal Recruits are a powerful defensive [[Cards|card]] because of how they are deployed, allowing good defensive [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to come from both lanes.
*The Evolved Royal Recruits should never be ignored as they will destroy both [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]] when left alone. This goes for any [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|tower troop]].
*The Evolved Royal Recruits are best used when on defense because they can easily defend both lanes, and apply a threatening counterpush when their shields are knocked off.
*Despite their horizontal formation, they can be split in slightly different ways by shifting the central tile of their deployment pattern to the left or right. This can cause 4 Evolved Royal Recruits to go in one lane and 2 in the other lane as opposed to the usual even formation. This makes them a good choice for split lane pushes.
*Unlike other cards, the Evolved Royal Recruits cannot be placed in the opponent's territory if one Crown Tower has been destroyed. Instead, they need both Crown Towers to be destroyed to be placed in the opponent's territory.
*The Evolved Royal Recruits have great synergy with the [[Royal Hogs]] as the Royal Hogs will entice a strong spell, such as [[Fireball]], from the opponent, knocking off their shields and causing them to charge. The Evolved Royal Recruits can tank for the Royal Hogs after the Fireball, allowing them to get damage on the Crown Tower.
*The best way to counter the Evolved Royal Recruits is to use a card that deals area damage, such as an [[Executioner]], [[Wizard]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Sparky]], [[Bomber]], Valkyrie, [[Ice Wizard]], [[Baby Dragon]], Mega Knight, [[Magic Archer]], [[Princess]], Firecracker [[Royal Ghost]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], Dark Prince, [[Witch]], or Bowler, and a tank, such as an [[Prince]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Monk]], Valkyrie, [[Miner]], [[Golden Knight]], or [[Knight]], in between your Crown Towers. This will make the Evolved Royal Recruits group up and make it easier to hit each Evolved Royal Recruit. Other cards, such as a combination of [[Bomb Tower]] and [[Valkyrie]], can achieve the same feat.
*[[:Category:Spell Cards|Spells]] are very situational counters to the Evolved Royal Recruits as their shields will absorb the spell's damage without harming the unit itself. Once the shields are knocked off, then a strong spell like Fireball, can be used to take them out as they charge.
*[[Arrows]] have a great synergy with the Evolved Royal Recruits as the Arrows will easily take out any fragile swarm, such as [[Skeleton Army]], [[Bats]], and [[Goblin Gang]], or ranged unit, such as [[Firecracker]], [[Princess]], Bomber, [[Archers]], [[Spear Goblins]], and [[Dart Goblin]], your opponent might place to counter them.
*Because of their horizontal formation, they can be used defensively even against splash units. This is especially useful against the [[Mega Knight]] or the [[Dark Prince]], as their formation minimizes the number of Royal Recruits that are hit by a single attack from the Mega Knight or Dark Prince.
*Due to their shields absorbing the damage, the Evolved Royal Recruits are very strong at taking the Giant Bomb from a [[Giant Skeleton]]. Additionally, they will begin charging, putting the opponent in a difficult situation.
*Since they cannot attack air troops, they can be weakened by splitting air swarms, like the [[Bats]], [[Minion Horde]], and [[Skeleton Dragons]]. However, note that this will allow them to charge due to their shields being destroyed, so only try this if the air swarms are supported with a ground distraction.
*The Evolved Royal Recruits have a slightly longer range than other melee troops, thus allowing them to safely attack distracted lower-range non-splash and splash cards alike, such as the [[Skeletons/Evolution|Evolved Skeletons]] and Valkyrie, without taking damage in return.
*Despite their charging, a lone [[Bowler]] can easily stop 1 lane of Evolved Royal Recruits when aligned with them. If he is placed in the center of the player's territory and combined with another card like an Ice Golem, he is able to fully stop both lanes.

